{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "03", "m": "09", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "06", "M": "37", "S": "08"}}, "news": [{"title": "West Bengal completes survey of 54.6 lakh households for PMAY", "para": "The P&RD department of West Bengal has successfully conducted a comprehensive survey of over 54.6 lakh households under the Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana. The innovative smartphone self-survey initiative has garnered nearly seven lakh applications, illustrating its popularity. Notably, South 24 Parganas district emerged as the leader in identifying over 4.8 lakh households, surpassing the projected survey completion by 123 percent.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/west-bengal-completes-survey-of-54-6-lakh-households-for-pmay/133725049?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-134078/133725049.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}, {"title": "Karnataka plans $400 billion Bengaluru region economy by 2037", "para": "Karnataka plans to expand Bengaluru's economy to $400 billion by 2037. The master plan aims to create millions of new jobs and boost key sectors. It seeks to drive private investment and finance urban transformation through land value capture. The region will be developed as a global hub for technology and advanced manufacturing. Public transport expansion and water security are also key components of this ambitious plan.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/karnataka-plans-400-billion-bengaluru-region-economy-by-2037/133724965?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-153162/133724965.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}, {"title": "Illegal floors, land use in Madhya Pradesh to now draw GIS glare", "para": "Madhya Pradesh has unveiled GARUD, a pioneering GIS-enabled online platform designed for citizens to report building plan violations and unauthorized constructions discreetly. By consolidating municipal and utility data, the system enhances urban management. Additionally, GARUD facilitates compliance checks for aviation and heritage zones concerning new constructions. Its innovative design has earned it an Achievement in GIS Award, recognizing its significant contribution to urban planning.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/technology/illegal-floors-land-use-in-madhya-pradesh-to-now-draw-gis-glare/133724873?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-144806/133724873.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "technology"}]}